{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:28:25", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-97ebe11c-1040-4f71-bdc0-bc3de1730a96', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Recovery Agent System"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011t4vJ84Dw2WjVh4c7T5edZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Gy5tX8D3dfuLQ4jSvJtPmD', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011t4vJ84Dw2WjVh4c7T5edZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Recovery Agent System Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy pane rather than keeping them isolated in the recovery dashboard.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when jobs are recovered through the recovery system:\\n1. Jobs run in a separate recovery context via `RecoveryOrchestrator._retry_agent()`\\n2. Recovered jobs are not visible in the main Agent Hierarchy tree on the Activity view\\n3. The recovery pane shows job status, but jobs may run to completion without appearing in the main UI\\n4. Users cannot track recovered jobs with the same visibility as regular jobs\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a `recovery_agent.md` agent definition in the `leadership/` directory\\n2. Modify the recovery orchestration to spawn Executive Directors via this Recovery Agent for each recovered job\\n3. Ensure recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs\\n4. Maintain visibility into recovery status while integrating with the main workflow\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n- Create a new agent type `leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- The Recovery Agent should:\\n  - Accept recovery task information (failed agent details, failure reason, recovery strategy)\\n  - Spawn an Executive Director to manage the recovered task\\n  - Pass the original user_vision/task to the Executive Director\\n  - Track recovery attempts and escalation history\\n\\n### FR2: Recovery Agent Capabilities\\n- **Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\\n- **Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers or coordinators (must go through Executive Director)\\n- **Input**: Recovery task details from the recovery queue\\n- **Output**: Status of recovery attempt, spawned Executive Director ID\\n\\n### FR3: Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Modify `swarm_recovery.py` to:\\n  - Use spawn_agent tool to spawn Recovery Agent instead of directly calling `_retry_agent`\\n  - Pass necessary context: original input_data, failure reason, recovery strategy\\n  - The Recovery Agent then spawns Executive Director with proper swarm state registration\\n\\n### FR4: Swarm State Integration\\n- Recovered jobs must:\\n  - Register in swarm_state as new agents with proper parent relationships\\n  - Appear in the `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint response\\n  - Be visible in the AgentHierarchyTree component\\n  - Link back to the original failed job via metadata\\n\\n### FR5: UI Visibility\\n- No UI changes required (feature request is backend-focused)\\n- Existing AgentHierarchyTree will automatically show recovered jobs once they\'re in swarm_state\\n- Recovery Dashboard can continue to show recovery-specific status info\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR1: Backward Compatibility\\n- Existing recovery dashboard should continue to work\\n- Recovery queue and history should still be populated\\n\\n### NFR2: Traceability\\n- Each recovery attempt should maintain reference to:\\n  - Original failed agent_id\\n  - Recovery queue entry\\n  - Failure reason and strategy applied\\n\\n## Technical Design Notes\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n    \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - ID of the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"original_session_id\\": \\"string - Session that contained the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"agent_type\\": \\"string - Type of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"agent_name\\": \\"string - Name of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"input_data\\": \\"object - Original input to the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"string - Why the agent failed/stalled\\",\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": \\"integer - Which recovery attempt this is\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"output_directory\\": \\"string - Where to write artifacts\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"recovery_id\\": \\"string - ID of this recovery attempt\\",\\n  \\"spawned_executive_id\\": \\"string - ID of the Executive Director spawned\\",\\n  \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - Reference to original failed agent\\",\\n  \\"message\\": \\"string - Status message\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"string - Performance analysis\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The Recovery Agent will be spawned by the RecoveryOrchestrator (which will need access to spawn_agent)\\n- The Executive Director spawned for recovery will create a new session or join existing session\\n- Recovery tasks will be visible both in recovery dashboard AND agent hierarchy\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\\n2. Users can track recovery progress the same way they track regular job progress\\n3. Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\\n4. No regression in existing recovery functionality\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Gy5tX8D3dfuLQ4jSvJtPmD', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/brass-band-achievements", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/css_accessibility_analysis_report.md", "tests/runtime/agents/test_brass_band_achievements.py"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "56 seconds ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "56 seconds ago"}, {"hash": "a81afe1939da863370999b4c3bff0b885cdea04a", "message": "Executive Director: Complete UI readability fix project for Improve page", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "dbb4e5cdf62e28d6aa04d1d80ad96ffa174e4b4c", "message": "Complete milestone 2: UI readability fix implementation and testing", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "91abbd5a22e7ab7748eb34750e92010366b3de1f", "message": "Complete milestone 1: UI readability analysis and architecture planning", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "85 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "92d30084e33cc181990ccee0a29990edf61fe10b", "message": "Implement whimsicalNames utility module with arrays, hash function, name generation, and emoji mapping", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "86 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RmJgkiPBBg97ZcWJvesf2V', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Recovery Agent System - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy.\n\n## Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure\n**Duration**: Sprint 1\n**Objective**: Create the Recovery Agent definition and establish the foundation for agent-based recovery\n\n### Deliverables\n1. `leadership/recovery_agent.md` - Agent definition file\n2. Input/output format validation for recovery tasks\n3. Unit tests for Recovery Agent definition parsing\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Recovery Agent definition follows existing agent format patterns\n- [ ] Agent can accept recovery task input format as specified\n- [ ] Agent can spawn Executive Director only (permission enforcement)\n- [ ] Agent outputs match defined output format\n- [ ] Tests pass for agent definition validation\n\n### Dependencies\n- None (foundational milestone)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: RecoveryOrchestrator Integration\n**Duration**: Sprint 2\n**Objective**: Modify the recovery orchestration to use the new Recovery Agent\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Modified `swarm_recovery.py` to spawn Recovery Agent\n2. Recovery Agent spawning Executive Director with proper context\n3. Integration tests for the recovery flow\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] RecoveryOrchestrator spawns Recovery Agent instead of direct retry\n- [ ] Recovery Agent successfully spawns Executive Director\n- [ ] Original task context is properly passed through the chain\n- [ ] Recovery attempt tracking is maintained\n- [ ] No regression in existing recovery functionality\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 1 complete (Recovery Agent definition exists)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 3: Swarm State Integration & Visibility\n**Duration**: Sprint 3\n**Objective**: Ensure recovered jobs appear in the agent hierarchy\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Proper swarm_state registration for recovery-spawned agents\n2. Parent-child relationship mapping for recovered agents\n3. Metadata preservation (original failure, attempt count)\n4. End-to-end integration tests\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Recovered jobs register in swarm_state with proper relationships\n- [ ] `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint includes recovered jobs\n- [ ] AgentHierarchyTree automatically displays recovered jobs\n- [ ] Recovery metadata is preserved and accessible\n- [ ] Original failed agent ID is linked in metadata\n- [ ] All tests pass including end-to-end scenarios\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 2 complete (Recovery Agent can spawn Executive Directors)\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### Technical Risks\n1. **Swarm State Timing**: Recovery agents must register before children spawn\n   - Mitigation: Ensure synchronous registration in spawn flow\n\n2. **Session Management**: Recovered jobs may need new sessions\n   - Mitigation: Allow flexible session handling in Recovery Agent\n\n3. **Backward Compatibility**: Existing recovery dashboard must continue working\n   - Mitigation: Add new functionality without removing existing hooks\n\n### Dependencies\n- Existing agent definition infrastructure must support new agent type\n- spawn_agent tool must be accessible from RecoveryOrchestrator context\n\n---\n\n## Success Metrics\n1. Recovered jobs visible in Agent Hierarchy (primary goal)\n2. No regression in recovery dashboard functionality\n3. Full traceability from original failure to recovery attempt\n4. All acceptance tests passing\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RmJgkiPBBg97ZcWJvesf2V', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_232429.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_232429.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XiSK3grf8MxswJKioFtUBS', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Recovery Agent System'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XiSK3grf8MxswJKioFtUBS', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Wk1saurh3DxvpN7GRtDvYS', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Recovery Agent System'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Wk1saurh3DxvpN7GRtDvYS', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011mtv4dYmVrXLwFVH4gKjXB', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011mtv4dYmVrXLwFVH4gKjXB', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: UI Readability Fix for Improve Page\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted remediation architecture** for fixing text readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach focuses on CSS specificity corrections and conditional styling improvements rather than a major architectural redesign.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-level styling fix with cascading CSS improvements\\n**Rationale**: This is a focused bug fix that requires minimal changes to preserve existing functionality while solving the specific contrast problem. A surgical approach ensures no unintended side effects.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n**No new technologies required** - this fix works within the existing stack:\\n\\n### Frontend (Existing)\\n- **React** - Component framework (already in use)\\n- **Bootstrap 5** - CSS framework with built-in color system (leveraging existing theme)\\n- **CSS-in-JS/Inline Styles** - Current styling approach in the component\\n\\n### Why This Approach\\n- **Minimal Risk**: Works with existing technology and patterns\\n- **Fast Implementation**: No new dependencies or learning curve\\n- **Maintainable**: Uses Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes for consistency\\n- **Tested**: Bootstrap\'s color combinations are accessibility-tested\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered:**\\n- CSS Modules: Overkill for a single component fix\\n- Styled Components: Would require major refactoring\\n- New CSS Framework: Unnecessary complexity for a readability fix\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Core Component\\n**SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx**\\n- **Current State**: Contains conditional styling that causes contrast issues\\n- **Responsibility**: Display performance analytics with proper text contrast\\n- **Fix Strategy**: Update styling logic to ensure text colors adapt with background changes\\n\\n### Styling Architecture\\n```\\nSelfImprovementDashboard\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Normal Mode Styling (light backgrounds)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-light, text-dark)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (semantic colors with proper text)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (standard contrast)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 \\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling (dark/danger backgrounds)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-danger, text-white)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (light variants with dark text)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (inverted contrast)\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n```\\nUser Interaction \\u2192 Mode State Change \\u2192 Conditional Styling Logic \\u2192 DOM Update \\u2192 Visual Rendering\\n```\\nNo changes to data flow - only styling application logic.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n**Files to Modify:**\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx  [PRIMARY TARGET]\\n```\\n\\n**Additional Files (if needed):**\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 dashboard-overrides.css  [IF NEEDED - for complex overrides]\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeHelpers.js  [IF NEEDED - for styling logic extraction]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**No database changes required** - this is purely a presentation layer fix.\\n\\n**State Management:**\\n- Existing component state (bumpers mode, performance data) remains unchanged\\n- Only CSS class application logic needs modification\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API changes required** - this fix is entirely frontend styling.\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Process\\n1. **Local Development**: Test fixes in development server\\n2. **Visual Testing**: Verify contrast in both light and dark modes\\n3. **Accessibility Testing**: Use browser dev tools to verify WCAG compliance\\n4. **Cross-Browser Testing**: Ensure fixes work in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n### Deployment\\n- **Type**: Frontend-only deployment\\n- **Risk Level**: Low (isolated component changes)\\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Git revert of specific styling changes\\n- **Testing Required**: Visual regression testing\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\nNo environment-specific configuration needed - styles apply universally.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Manual test cases:\\n1. Load Improve page in normal mode\\n   \\u2192 Verify all text is readable against backgrounds\\n2. Enable \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode  \\n   \\u2192 Verify danger theme maintains text contrast\\n3. Test responsive breakpoints\\n   \\u2192 Ensure readability on mobile/tablet/desktop\\n```\\n\\n### Automated Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Accessibility tests (if jest-axe available):\\ndescribe(\'SelfImprovementDashboard Accessibility\', () => {\\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in normal mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test WCAG compliance\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in bumpers off mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test danger theme compliance\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Browser Testing\\n- **Chrome**: Primary development browser\\n- **Firefox**: Secondary testing\\n- **Safari**: macOS compatibility\\n- **Edge**: Windows compatibility\\n\\n## Specific Technical Implementation\\n\\n### Bootstrap Color Strategy\\n```jsx\\n// Current problematic pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-muted\\">Problem text</span> // This creates dark on dark\\n</Card>\\n\\n// Fixed pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-light\\">Readable text</span>\\n</Card>\\n```\\n\\n### Conditional Styling Logic\\n```jsx\\nconst getTextClass = (isDangerMode, baseClass) => {\\n  if (isDangerMode) {\\n    return baseClass.includes(\'dark\') ? \'text-white\' : \'text-light\';\\n  }\\n  return baseClass.includes(\'light\') ? \'text-dark\' : \'text-white\';\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Option 1: Complete CSS Framework Migration\\n**Rejected**: Too much risk for a simple contrast fix\\n\\n### Option 2: Custom Design System\\n**Rejected**: Overkill - Bootstrap\'s accessibility features solve this when used correctly\\n\\n### Option 3: JavaScript-based Theme Switching\\n**Rejected**: Adds complexity when CSS classes can solve the issue\\n\\n### Option 4: CSS Variables for Dynamic Theming\\n**Considered**: Good for future scalability, but unnecessary for this focused fix\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Breaking Existing Visual Design\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes\\n- Test both modes thoroughly\\n- Take screenshots for before/after comparison\\n\\n### Risk 2: CSS Specificity Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use inline styles for high specificity when needed\\n- Follow existing patterns in the codebase\\n- Test in actual browser environment\\n\\n### Risk 3: Performance Impact\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- No new CSS files or frameworks\\n- Minimal additional class computations\\n- No impact on bundle size\\n\\n### Risk 4: Cross-Browser Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use standard Bootstrap classes (well-tested across browsers)\\n- Test in multiple browsers\\n- Avoid custom CSS properties that might not be supported\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Design Questions for User Review\\n1. **Color Preference**: Should danger mode use red backgrounds with white text, or prefer orange/yellow for better accessibility?\\n2. **Badge Styling**: For dark badges, prefer white text or switch to light-colored badges with dark text?\\n3. **Table Styling**: In dark mode, prefer inverted table colors or maintain current table style with better text contrast?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input\\n1. **Approach**: Pure inline styling vs. conditional CSS classes?\\n2. **Scope**: Fix only the reported component or audit entire application for similar issues?\\n3. **Testing**: Include automated accessibility tests or rely on manual verification?\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Immediate Fix (1-2 hours)\\n- Identify and fix the most critical contrast issues\\n- Focus on badges and card text\\n- Test both normal and danger modes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Comprehensive Audit (2-3 hours)\\n- Review all text elements in the component\\n- Ensure WCAG compliance\\n- Add consistent styling patterns\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing and Validation (1 hour)\\n- Cross-browser testing\\n- Accessibility validation\\n- User acceptance testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Contrast Ratio**: All text meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large)\\n2. **Visual Verification**: User confirms readability issues are resolved\\n3. **No Regression**: All existing functionality works unchanged\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable impact on page load or rendering performance\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **User Approval**: Confirm this architectural approach before implementation\\n2. **Development**: Implement the CSS fixes following this plan\\n3. **Testing**: Execute the testing strategy outlined above\\n4. **Deployment**: Deploy with the low-risk strategy described\\n\\nThis architecture provides a focused, low-risk solution that addresses the specific readability problem while maintaining system stability and existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VQ2DuM31wP7KHGxAEPcHaT', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture: Recovery Agent System\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nThis architecture introduces a **Recovery Agent** into the agent hierarchy to govern job recovery. The key innovation is replacing direct retry mechanisms with agent-spawned recovery, ensuring recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs.\n\n**Architecture Pattern**: Agent-based Recovery Orchestration\n**Rationale**: By treating recovery as a first-class agent-spawned operation, recovered jobs automatically integrate with existing swarm state tracking, hierarchy visualization, and monitoring infrastructure.\n\n## System Components\n\n### 1. Recovery Agent (`leadership/recovery_agent.md`)\n**Role**: Specialized leadership agent that governs recovery operations\n**Responsibilities**:\n- Accept recovery task information from RecoveryOrchestrator\n- Spawn Executive Directors to handle recovered tasks\n- Track recovery attempts and maintain metadata\n- Report recovery status back to orchestrator\n\n**Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\n**Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers, coordinators, or other agents\n\n### 2. Modified RecoveryOrchestrator (`swarm_recovery.py`)\n**Role**: Orchestrates recovery queue processing\n**Changes Required**:\n- Instead of calling `_retry_agent()` directly, spawn Recovery Agent via `spawn_agent` tool\n- Pass recovery context (original input, failure reason, strategy) to Recovery Agent\n- Monitor spawned Recovery Agent for completion\n\n### 3. Swarm State Integration\n**Role**: Existing infrastructure, minimal changes needed\n**Requirement**: Recovery Agent and its spawned Executive Directors must register properly\n**Behavior**: Once agents register in swarm_state, they automatically appear in hierarchy API\n\n## Data Flow\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        CURRENT FLOW (TO BE REPLACED)                     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                          │\n│  RecoveryOrchestrator                                                    │\n│         │                                                                │\n│         ▼                                                                │\n│  _retry_agent() ──────► Direct Agent Spawn                               │\n│         │                    (No swarm_state registration)               │\n│         ▼                                                                │\n│  Recovery Dashboard Only                                                 │\n│  (Jobs NOT visible in hierarchy)                                         │\n│                                                                          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        NEW FLOW (TO BE IMPLEMENTED)                      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                          │\n│  RecoveryOrchestrator                                                    │\n│         │                                                                │\n│         │ spawn_agent("leadership/recovery_agent", recovery_task)        │\n│         ▼                                                                │\n│  ┌─────────────────┐                                                     │\n│  │ Recovery Agent  │ ◄──── Registers in swarm_state                      │\n│  │ (leadership/)   │                                                     │\n│  └────────┬────────┘                                                     │\n│           │                                                              │\n│           │ spawn_agent("leadership/executive_director", original_task)  │\n│           ▼                                                              │\n│  ┌───────────────────────┐                                               │\n│  │  Executive Director   │ ◄──── Registers in swarm_state                │\n│  │  (recovered task)     │       Parent: Recovery Agent                  │\n│  └────────┬──────────────┘                                               │\n│           │                                                              │\n│           ▼ (normal ED workflow)                                         │\n│  ┌───────────────────────┐                                               │\n│  │  Dev Manager, etc.    │ ◄──── All children visible in hierarchy       │\n│  └───────────────────────┘                                               │\n│                                                                          │\n│  Result: All agents visible in Agent Hierarchy Tree                      │\n│          + Recovery Dashboard still shows recovery-specific info         │\n│                                                                          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## File/Directory Structure\n\n### New Files to Create\n```\nsrc/\n└── ensemble/\n    └── docs/\n        └── agents/\n            └── leadership/\n                └── recovery_agent.md    # New agent definition\n```\n\n### Files to Modify\n```\nsrc/\n└── ensemble/\n    └── runtime/\n        └── swarm_recovery.py    # Use spawn_agent instead of direct retry\n```\n\n### No Changes Required\n```\nsrc/\n└── field/\n    └── ensemble_ui/\n        └── backend/\n            └── routes/\n                └── activity.py   # Hierarchy endpoint already works\n        └── frontend/\n            └── src/\n                └── components/\n                    └── AgentHierarchyTree.jsx  # Already displays swarm_state\n```\n\n## Recovery Agent Definition\n\n### Input Format\n```json\n{\n  "recovery_task": {\n    "original_agent_id": "string - ID of the failed agent",\n    "original_session_id": "string - Session that contained the failed agent",\n    "agent_type": "string - Type of agent that failed",\n    "agent_name": "string - Name of agent that failed",\n    "input_data": "object - Original input to the failed agent",\n    "failure_reason": "string - Why the agent failed/stalled",\n    "recovery_strategy": "string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)",\n    "recovery_attempt": "integer - Which recovery attempt this is"\n  },\n  "output_directory": "string - Where to write artifacts"\n}\n```\n\n### Output Format\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "recovery_id": "string - ID of this recovery attempt",\n  "spawned_executive_id": "string - ID of the Executive Director spawned",\n  "original_agent_id": "string - Reference to original failed agent",\n  "message": "string - Status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - Performance analysis"\n}\n```\n\n### Agent Definition Structure\n```markdown\n# Recovery Agent\n\n## Purpose\nGoverns job recovery by spawning Executive Directors for recovered tasks.\n\n## Instructions\n1. Receive recovery task from RecoveryOrchestrator\n2. Extract original input_data and task context\n3. Spawn Executive Director with original task + recovery metadata\n4. Monitor Executive Director completion\n5. Report recovery status\n\n## Permissions\n- can_spawn: ["leadership/executive_director"]\n- can_write_code: false\n\n## Input Format\n(as above)\n\n## Output Format\n(as above)\n```\n\n## API Changes\n\n### No New Endpoints Required\nThe existing `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint will automatically include recovered jobs once they register in swarm_state.\n\n### Metadata Enhancement\nRecovery-spawned agents should include metadata:\n```json\n{\n  "agent_id": "recovery-exec-abc123",\n  "agent_type": "leadership/executive_director",\n  "metadata": {\n    "is_recovery": true,\n    "original_failed_agent_id": "original-abc123",\n    "recovery_attempt": 1,\n    "recovery_strategy": "retry",\n    "failure_reason": "timeout"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Integration Points\n\n### RecoveryOrchestrator Changes\n```python\n# BEFORE (swarm_recovery.py)\nasync def _process_recovery_task(self, task):\n    await self._retry_agent(task)  # Direct retry, no hierarchy integration\n\n# AFTER\nasync def _process_recovery_task(self, task):\n    recovery_input = {\n        "recovery_task": {\n            "original_agent_id": task.agent_id,\n            "original_session_id": task.session_id,\n            "agent_type": task.agent_type,\n            "agent_name": task.agent_name,\n            "input_data": task.input_data,\n            "failure_reason": task.failure_reason,\n            "recovery_strategy": task.recovery_strategy,\n            "recovery_attempt": task.attempt_count\n        },\n        "output_directory": self.output_directory\n    }\n    \n    # Spawn Recovery Agent (which spawns ED, which registers in swarm_state)\n    result = await self.spawn_agent(\n        "leadership/recovery_agent",\n        recovery_input\n    )\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests\n1. Recovery Agent definition parsing\n2. Input/output format validation\n3. Permission enforcement (can only spawn ED)\n\n### Integration Tests\n1. RecoveryOrchestrator → Recovery Agent spawning\n2. Recovery Agent → Executive Director spawning\n3. Swarm state registration verification\n\n### End-to-End Tests\n1. Trigger a recoverable failure\n2. Verify job enters recovery queue\n3. Verify Recovery Agent spawns\n4. Verify Executive Director appears in hierarchy\n5. Verify recovery metadata preserved\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\n### Preserved Functionality\n- Recovery queue continues to work\n- Recovery dashboard continues to show recovery status\n- Recovery history is still populated\n- Existing UI components unchanged\n\n### New Behavior\n- Recovered jobs NOW also appear in Agent Hierarchy\n- Recovery metadata available in hierarchy view\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: spawn_agent Availability\n**Issue**: RecoveryOrchestrator may not have access to spawn_agent tool\n**Mitigation**: Ensure RecoveryOrchestrator runs in a context with tool access, or create a spawning utility\n\n### Risk 2: Session Management\n**Issue**: Recovered jobs may create orphaned sessions\n**Mitigation**: Recovery Agent should reuse existing session or create with proper parent reference\n\n### Risk 3: Infinite Recovery Loops\n**Issue**: Recovery Agent could fail, triggering more recovery\n**Mitigation**: Mark Recovery Agent as non-recoverable or add loop detection\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n1. ✅ When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\n2. ✅ Users can track recovery progress the same way as regular jobs\n3. ✅ Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\n4. ✅ No regression in existing recovery functionality\n5. ✅ All tests pass\n\n## Open Questions (None - Decisions Made)\n\n1. **Session handling**: Recovery Agent creates new session linked to recovery queue entry\n2. **Recovery Agent failures**: Mark Recovery Agent as non-recoverable to prevent loops\n3. **UI changes**: None required - existing UI auto-displays registered agents\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VQ2DuM31wP7KHGxAEPcHaT', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260114_232550.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260114_232550.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019UtVTqZYyBZuk2PZiGCr2X', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure - Create the recovery_agent.md agent definition file and establish the foundation for agent-based recovery. Includes input/output format validation.', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01HKE3C2xXVMjsWzag5Xnwc7', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/test_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure - Create tests for the recovery_agent.md agent definition parsing, input/output format validation, and permission enforcement (can only spawn Executive Director).', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019UtVTqZYyBZuk2PZiGCr2X', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 11, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1.1 \\u2192 Task 1.2, Task 1.3 (agent definition provides specification for schemas)", "Task 1.2, Task 1.3 \\u2192 Task 2.1 (schemas required for validation utility)", "Task 2.1 \\u2192 Task 2.2 (validation utility required for spawn integration)", "Task 1.2, Task 1.3 \\u2192 Task 3.1 (schemas required for test fixtures)", "Task 3.1, Task 2.1 \\u2192 Task 3.2 (fixtures and validation required for unit tests)", "Task 2.2, Task 3.1 \\u2192 Task 3.3 (spawn integration and fixtures required for integration tests)", "Task 1.1, Task 1.2, Task 1.3 \\u2192 Task 4.1 (agent definition and schemas required for usage docs)", "Task 2.1, Task 2.2 \\u2192 Task 4.2 (validation infrastructure required for developer docs)"], "message": "Successfully identified 11 backend tasks across 4 task groups for Milestone 1. Tasks cover: (1) Recovery Agent definition and I/O schemas, (2) validation infrastructure with agent spawn integration, (3) comprehensive testing with fixtures and test suites, (4) documentation for usage and developer guides. Critical path: Task 1.1 \\u2192 1.2 \\u2192 2.1 \\u2192 2.2 \\u2192 3.3. All tasks have clear acceptance criteria, are TDD-ready, and include technical implementation details. No clarification needed - standard FastAPI/Pydantic patterns apply."}}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01HKE3C2xXVMjsWzag5Xnwc7', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "completed", "response_type": "conversational", "message": "Now I\'ll analyze the architecture and requirements to create a comprehensive test strategy for Milestone 1.", "agent": "Test Coordinator"}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QRUjD2bHgHP8CZPW2ESBzR', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VcMGSFQK541cgGAX9sfEGP', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QRUjD2bHgHP8CZPW2ESBzR', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Backend Tasks - Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis milestone establishes the foundation for agent-based recovery by creating the Recovery Agent definition and implementing input/output format validation. This is the foundational work that enables recovered jobs to appear in the main agent hierarchy.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n\\n### Task 1.1: Create Recovery Agent Definition File\\n**Description**: Create the `recovery_agent.md` agent definition file in the leadership directory following the standard agent definition format.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- File created at `src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- Contains all required sections: Purpose, Instructions, Permissions, Input Format, Output Format, Termination Conditions\\n- Input format matches specification (recovery_task object + output_directory)\\n- Output format matches specification (status, recovery_id, spawned_executive_id, etc.)\\n- Permissions explicitly set: `can_spawn: [\\"leadership/executive_director\\"]`, `can_write_code: false`, `can_write_tests: false`\\n- Instructions clearly define: receive recovery task \\u2192 spawn Executive Director \\u2192 monitor completion \\u2192 report status\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Follow existing agent definition patterns from `docs/agents/leadership/`\\n- Include recovery-specific workflow steps\\n- Document error handling expectations\\n- Specify metadata requirements for recovery tracking\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 1.2: Create Recovery Agent Input Validation Schema\\n**Description**: Create Pydantic models for validating Recovery Agent input format, ensuring all required fields are present and correctly typed.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryTaskInput` created for the recovery_task object\\n- Fields validated: original_agent_id (str), original_session_id (str), agent_type (str), agent_name (str), input_data (dict), failure_reason (str), recovery_strategy (str), recovery_attempt (int)\\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryAgentInput` created wrapping recovery_task + output_directory\\n- Validation includes: required field checks, type validation, string min/max lengths where appropriate\\n- All validation errors return clear messages indicating which field failed and why\\n- Unit tests cover: valid input, missing fields, wrong types, invalid values\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1 (definition file provides specification)\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Create in `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py` (new file)\\n- Use Pydantic v2 syntax with Field validators\\n- recovery_strategy should be an enum: [\\"retry\\", \\"enhance_prompt\\", \\"escalate\\"]\\n- recovery_attempt must be positive integer\\n- input_data is dict with no schema (flexible for any agent type)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 1.3: Create Recovery Agent Output Validation Schema\\n**Description**: Create Pydantic models for validating Recovery Agent output format, ensuring consistent response structure.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryAgentOutput` created\\n- Fields validated: status (enum: success/failed/needs_user_input), recovery_id (str), spawned_executive_id (str), original_agent_id (str), message (str), self_analysis (str)\\n- All fields required except self_analysis (optional)\\n- Status enum properly defined and enforced\\n- Unit tests cover: valid output, missing fields, invalid status values\\n- Output validation integrated with agent response handling\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1 (definition file provides specification)\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Add to `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py`\\n- Status enum: `RecoveryStatus = Literal[\\"success\\", \\"failed\\", \\"needs_user_input\\"]`\\n- recovery_id and spawned_executive_id should follow UUID format (add validator)\\n- self_analysis defaults to empty string if not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 2: Validation Infrastructure\\n\\n### Task 2.1: Create Validation Utility for Agent I/O\\n**Description**: Create a generic utility function that validates agent inputs and outputs against their defined schemas, usable by the Recovery Agent and future agents.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Function `validate_agent_input(agent_type: str, input_data: dict) -> tuple[bool, dict|str]` created\\n- Function `validate_agent_output(agent_type: str, output_data: dict) -> tuple[bool, dict|str]` created\\n- Functions return (success: bool, validated_data_or_error_message)\\n- Schema registry maps agent types to their Pydantic models\\n- Recovery Agent schemas registered in the registry\\n- Unit tests cover: valid data, invalid data, unknown agent type, malformed JSON\\n- Error messages are descriptive and actionable\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2, Task 1.3\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Create `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/agent_validator.py` (new file)\\n- Schema registry: `AGENT_SCHEMAS = {\\"leadership/recovery_agent\\": {\\"input\\": RecoveryAgentInput, \\"output\\": RecoveryAgentOutput}}`\\n- Handle Pydantic ValidationError and return formatted error messages\\n- Cache schema instances for performance\\n- Future-proof: allow dynamic schema registration\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 2.2: Integrate Validation into Agent Spawn Pipeline\\n**Description**: Hook the validation utility into the agent spawning process so that input validation occurs before spawning and output validation occurs after completion.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- `spawn_agent` function validates input using `validate_agent_input` before spawning\\n- If validation fails, spawn_agent returns error without spawning agent\\n- Agent completion handler validates output using `validate_agent_output`\\n- If output validation fails, log warning but don\'t block (agent already completed)\\n- Validation errors logged with agent_type, input/output data, and specific validation failure\\n- Integration tests verify validation occurs at correct points in lifecycle\\n- Metrics tracked: validation_failures_total (by agent_type, validation_type: input/output)\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Modify `src/ensemble/runtime/agent_spawner.py` (or equivalent spawning logic)\\n- Add validation call before `Agent.create()` or equivalent\\n- Add validation call in agent completion callback/handler\\n- Use existing logging infrastructure for validation errors\\n- Consider: Add `skip_validation=False` parameter for backwards compatibility during rollout\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 3: Testing Infrastructure\\n\\n### Task 3.1: Create Recovery Agent Test Fixtures\\n**Description**: Create pytest fixtures and test data generators for Recovery Agent testing.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Fixture `valid_recovery_task_input()` generates valid RecoveryAgentInput\\n- Fixture `invalid_recovery_task_input(field: str)` generates input with specified invalid field\\n- Fixture `valid_recovery_agent_output()` generates valid RecoveryAgentOutput\\n- Test data includes edge cases: very long strings, special characters, boundary integers\\n- Fixtures parameterizable (e.g., override specific fields)\\n- Documentation explains how to use fixtures in tests\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2, Task 1.3\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Create `tests/fixtures/recovery_agent_fixtures.py`\\n- Use factory pattern: `def recovery_task_factory(**overrides) -> dict`\\n- Include fixtures for all recovery strategies\\n- Include fixtures for all status values\\n- Ensure generated UUIDs are valid format\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 3.2: Create Validation Test Suite\\n**Description**: Comprehensive test suite for input/output validation covering all schemas and edge cases.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Test file `tests/unit/test_recovery_validation.py` created\\n- Tests for RecoveryTaskInput: valid input, each required field missing, each field wrong type, boundary values\\n- Tests for RecoveryAgentInput: valid input, missing output_directory, invalid paths\\n- Tests for RecoveryAgentOutput: valid output, each status value, missing required fields, invalid UUIDs\\n- Tests for validate_agent_input: valid, invalid, unknown agent type, malformed data\\n- Tests for validate_agent_output: valid, invalid, unknown agent type\\n- All tests pass with >95% code coverage on validation modules\\n- Tests use fixtures from Task 3.1\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1, Task 2.1\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Use pytest parametrize for testing multiple invalid field scenarios\\n- Test error messages are descriptive\\n- Test that Pydantic validation errors are properly caught and formatted\\n- Test edge cases: empty strings, null values, extremely large integers\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 3.3: Create Integration Test for Agent Spawn Validation\\n**Description**: Integration test verifying validation occurs correctly during the agent spawn lifecycle.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Test file `tests/integration/test_spawn_validation.py` created\\n- Test: Valid input passes validation and agent spawns successfully\\n- Test: Invalid input fails validation and agent does not spawn\\n- Test: Valid output passes validation silently\\n- Test: Invalid output logs warning but doesn\'t block\\n- Test: Unknown agent type skips validation (no schema registered)\\n- Mock agent spawning to avoid full agent execution\\n- Verify validation metrics are incremented correctly\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.2, Task 3.1\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Use pytest-mock for mocking spawn_agent internals\\n- Mock agent completion to control output validation testing\\n- Capture logs and verify validation error messages appear\\n- Mock metrics/telemetry and assert validation_failures_total incremented\\n- Test both sync and async spawn paths if applicable\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 4: Documentation & Examples\\n\\n### Task 4.1: Create Recovery Agent Usage Documentation\\n**Description**: Write documentation explaining how to use the Recovery Agent, including input/output examples and integration guidance.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Documentation file `docs/recovery_agent_usage.md` created\\n- Sections: Overview, Input Format (with examples), Output Format (with examples), Common Errors, Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Includes complete JSON examples of valid input and output\\n- Documents all recovery strategies and when to use each\\n- Explains error messages and how to fix validation failures\\n- Links to agent definition file and validation schemas\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1, Task 1.2, Task 1.3\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Use real examples from test fixtures\\n- Include code snippets showing how to spawn Recovery Agent\\n- Add flowchart showing Recovery Agent workflow\\n- Include troubleshooting section with common validation errors\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 4.2: Create Validation Schema Documentation\\n**Description**: Write developer documentation for the validation infrastructure, enabling other agents to adopt validation.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Documentation file `docs/agent_validation.md` created\\n- Sections: Overview, Creating Schemas, Registering Schemas, Testing Validation, Best Practices\\n- Step-by-step guide for adding validation to new agent types\\n- Example showing full validation implementation for a sample agent\\n- Documents the validation utility API\\n- Explains validation timing (pre-spawn, post-completion)\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1, Task 2.2\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Include code examples for creating Pydantic schemas\\n- Show how to register schemas in AGENT_SCHEMAS registry\\n- Document when to use strict vs lenient validation\\n- Explain error handling patterns\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Total Tasks**: 11\\n**Task Groups**: 4\\n\\n**Dependencies Chain**:\\n1. Foundation: Task 1.1 (agent definition)\\n2. Schemas: Task 1.2, 1.3 (input/output schemas)\\n3. Validation Infrastructure: Task 2.1 \\u2192 Task 2.2 (validation utilities \\u2192 integration)\\n4. Testing: Task 3.1 \\u2192 Task 3.2, Task 3.3 (fixtures \\u2192 tests)\\n5. Documentation: Task 4.1, Task 4.2 (parallel, depend on implementation tasks)\\n\\n**Critical Path**: \\nTask 1.1 \\u2192 Task 1.2 \\u2192 Task 2.1 \\u2192 Task 2.2 \\u2192 Task 3.3\\n\\n**Estimated Complexity**:\\n- Simple: 4 tasks\\n- Medium: 6 tasks\\n- Complex: 0 tasks\\n\\n**Key Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership/recovery_agent.md` - Agent definition\\n2. `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py` - Pydantic validation models\\n3. `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/agent_validator.py` - Validation utility\\n4. Integration with spawn pipeline for automatic validation\\n5. Comprehensive test suite with >95% coverage\\n6. Developer documentation for recovery agent and validation infrastructure\\n\\n**Ready for Handoff**: Yes - All tasks are well-defined, have clear acceptance criteria, and can be implemented via TDD by the TDD Coordinator.\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VcMGSFQK541cgGAX9sfEGP', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Strategy - Foundation Infrastructure Milestone\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis milestone establishes core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security. Testing focuses on validating the reliability, security, and robustness of fundamental systems that all future features will depend on.\\n\\n## Test Coverage Goals\\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 85% for business logic components\\n- **Integration Coverage**: 100% of all git operations, state persistence, and security functions\\n- **E2E Coverage**: Critical workflows for commit automation, branch management, and recovery scenarios\\n\\n## Testing Framework Stack\\n- **Backend**: pytest with mocks for external dependencies\\n- **Frontend**: Jest + React Testing Library\\n- **E2E**: Playwright for git workflow automation\\n- **Security**: Custom security tests for secrets management\\n- **Performance**: Load tests for state persistence under concurrent access\\n\\n## Core Components to Test\\n\\n### 1. Enhanced Git Operations\\n**Components**:\\n- `git_commit` enhanced tool with auto-formatting\\n- `git_branch` tool with milestone branch patterns\\n- `git_merge` tool with conflict resolution\\n- Commit message generation with agent attribution\\n\\n**Critical Business Logic**:\\n- Commit message formatting and agent attribution\\n- Branch naming conventions and validation\\n- Merge conflict detection and resolution strategies\\n- Git state validation before operations\\n\\n### 2. State Persistence & Recovery System\\n**Components**:\\n- Checkpoint creation and restoration\\n- Pipeline state serialization\\n- Recovery mechanism for interrupted operations\\n- State validation and integrity checks\\n\\n**Critical Business Logic**:\\n- State consistency across agent restarts\\n- Recovery point identification and rollback\\n- Concurrent access handling\\n- Data integrity validation\\n\\n### 3. Secrets Management\\n**Components**:\\n- API key secure storage and retrieval\\n- Credential encryption/decryption\\n- Access control and audit logging\\n- Integration with external secret stores\\n\\n**Critical Business Logic**:\\n- Encryption key management\\n- Access permission validation\\n- Secure credential rotation\\n- Audit trail generation\\n\\n## Test Task Breakdown\\n\\n### Unit Tests (22 tasks)\\n\\n#### Enhanced Git Operations (8 tasks)\\n**TASK-U001**: Test commit message generation with agent attribution\\n- Test agent metadata inclusion in commit messages\\n- Validate commit message formatting standards\\n- Mock git repository operations\\n\\n**TASK-U002**: Test branch name validation and formatting  \\n- Test milestone-based branch naming conventions\\n- Validate branch name sanitization\\n- Test invalid branch name rejection\\n\\n**TASK-U003**: Test git operation state validation\\n- Test pre-commit validation checks\\n- Test repository state assessment\\n- Mock git status operations\\n\\n**TASK-U004**: Test merge conflict detection logic\\n- Test conflict identification algorithms\\n- Test merge strategy selection\\n- Mock git merge scenarios\\n\\n**TASK-U005**: Test commit atomicity and rollback\\n- Test partial commit failure handling\\n- Test rollback mechanisms\\n- Mock git operation failures\\n\\n**TASK-U006**: Test branch creation with proper base selection\\n- Test base branch identification logic\\n- Test branch creation validation\\n- Mock branch hierarchy operations\\n\\n**TASK-U007**: Test git history analysis for auto-commit decisions\\n- Test commit frequency analysis\\n- Test change magnitude assessment\\n- Mock git log parsing\\n\\n**TASK-U008**: Test git operation permission validation\\n- Test repository access permissions\\n- Test operation authorization checks\\n- Mock permission denial scenarios\\n\\n#### State Persistence (8 tasks)\\n**TASK-U009**: Test checkpoint creation and serialization\\n- Test agent state serialization\\n- Test checkpoint data structure validation\\n- Mock file system operations\\n\\n**TASK-U010**: Test checkpoint restoration and deserialization\\n- Test state restoration accuracy\\n- Test data integrity validation\\n- Mock corrupted checkpoint handling\\n\\n**TASK-U011**: Test concurrent checkpoint access\\n- Test multi-agent checkpoint coordination\\n- Test lock mechanism functionality\\n- Mock concurrent access scenarios\\n\\n**TASK-U012**: Test state validation and integrity checks\\n- Test checksum validation\\n- Test state consistency verification\\n- Mock integrity failure scenarios\\n\\n**TASK-U013**: Test recovery point identification\\n- Test recovery point selection logic\\n- Test partial recovery scenarios\\n- Mock incomplete checkpoint data\\n\\n**TASK-U014**: Test pipeline state tracking\\n- Test agent progress tracking\\n- Test milestone completion detection\\n- Mock agent state transitions\\n\\n**TASK-U015**: Test cleanup and retention policies\\n- Test old checkpoint removal\\n- Test storage space management\\n- Mock storage limit scenarios\\n\\n**TASK-U016**: Test cross-agent state sharing\\n- Test shared state synchronization\\n- Test state conflict resolution\\n- Mock state merge scenarios\\n\\n#### Secrets Management (6 tasks)\\n**TASK-U017**: Test credential encryption/decryption\\n- Test encryption algorithm implementation\\n- Test key derivation functions\\n- Mock encryption key operations\\n\\n**TASK-U018**: Test access control validation\\n- Test permission-based access controls\\n- Test role-based authorization\\n- Mock unauthorized access attempts\\n\\n**TASK-U019**: Test secure storage operations\\n- Test credential storage mechanisms\\n- Test storage encryption validation\\n- Mock storage failure scenarios\\n\\n**TASK-U020**: Test credential rotation logic\\n- Test automatic credential updates\\n- Test rotation scheduling\\n- Mock credential provider APIs\\n\\n**TASK-U021**: Test audit logging functionality\\n- Test access event logging\\n- Test audit trail generation\\n- Mock logging system failures\\n\\n**TASK-U022**: Test secrets validation and health checks\\n- Test credential validity verification\\n- Test expired credential detection\\n- Mock credential validation APIs\\n\\n### Integration Tests (15 tasks)\\n\\n#### Git Workflow Integration (6 tasks)\\n**TASK-I001**: Test complete commit automation workflow\\n- Test end-to-end auto-commit process\\n- Integrate with real git repository\\n- Validate commit appears in git history\\n\\n**TASK-I002**: Test branch-based development workflow\\n- Test milestone branch creation to merge cycle\\n- Integrate with git repository structure\\n- Validate branch protection and merge requirements\\n\\n**TASK-I003**: Test merge conflict resolution integration\\n- Test conflict detection with real git scenarios\\n- Integrate conflict resolution with merge tools\\n- Validate successful merge completion\\n\\n**TASK-I004**: Test git operation error handling and recovery\\n- Test git command failure scenarios\\n- Integrate with error reporting systems\\n- Validate graceful failure recovery\\n\\n**TASK-I005**: Test concurrent git operations coordination\\n- Test multiple agents performing git operations\\n- Integrate with locking mechanisms\\n- Validate operation serialization\\n\\n**TASK-I006**: Test git history integration with state tracking\\n- Test commit history correlation with agent states\\n- Integrate git metadata with checkpoint system\\n- Validate historical state reconstruction\\n\\n#### State System Integration (5 tasks)\\n**TASK-I007**: Test state persistence with file system\\n- Test checkpoint file creation and retrieval\\n- Integrate with actual file system storage\\n- Validate data persistence across restarts\\n\\n**TASK-I008**: Test recovery system integration\\n- Test complete pipeline recovery from checkpoints\\n- Integrate with agent restart mechanisms\\n- Validate state consistency after recovery\\n\\n**TASK-I009**: Test state sharing between agents\\n- Test inter-agent state communication\\n- Integrate with message passing systems\\n- Validate state synchronization accuracy\\n\\n**TASK-I010**: Test state cleanup with storage systems\\n- Test automated cleanup processes\\n- Integrate with file system monitoring\\n- Validate storage space management\\n\\n**TASK-I011**: Test state validation with data integrity\\n- Test comprehensive state validation\\n- Integrate with data validation libraries\\n- Validate error detection and reporting\\n\\n#### Security Integration (4 tasks)\\n**TASK-I012**: Test secrets management with external providers\\n- Test integration with HashiCorp Vault or similar\\n- Integrate with API key management services\\n- Validate secure credential retrieval\\n\\n**TASK-I013**: Test encrypted storage integration\\n- Test credential encryption with storage systems\\n- Integrate with encryption libraries\\n- Validate data protection at rest\\n\\n**TASK-I014**: Test audit logging integration\\n- Test audit log generation and storage\\n- Integrate with logging infrastructure\\n- Validate audit trail completeness\\n\\n**TASK-I015**: Test security validation with authentication\\n- Test credential-based authentication flows\\n- Integrate with identity management systems\\n- Validate access control enforcement\\n\\n### End-to-End Tests (8 tasks)\\n\\n#### Critical User Journeys (8 tasks)\\n**TASK-E001**: Test complete milestone development workflow\\n- User creates milestone with multiple features\\n- Agents create branches, make commits, handle merges\\n- Validate entire workflow from start to delivery\\n\\n**TASK-E002**: Test pipeline failure and recovery scenario\\n- Simulate agent failure during development\\n- Test recovery from latest checkpoint\\n- Validate continuation without data loss\\n\\n**TASK-E003**: Test concurrent agent development workflow\\n- Multiple agents working on different features\\n- Test branch management and merge coordination\\n- Validate no conflicts or lost work\\n\\n**TASK-E004**: Test secrets rotation during active development\\n- API credentials expire during agent execution\\n- Test automatic credential refresh\\n- Validate uninterrupted agent operation\\n\\n**TASK-E005**: Test git conflict resolution workflow\\n- Agents create conflicting changes\\n- Test automatic conflict detection and resolution\\n- Validate successful merge completion\\n\\n**TASK-E006**: Test state corruption recovery\\n- Simulate checkpoint corruption\\n- Test fallback to previous valid state\\n- Validate minimal work loss\\n\\n**TASK-E007**: Test long-running development session\\n- Extended multi-agent development session\\n- Test checkpoint frequency and storage efficiency\\n- Validate system stability over time\\n\\n**TASK-E008**: Test security breach simulation\\n- Simulate unauthorized access attempt\\n- Test security controls and audit logging\\n- Validate system protection and alerting\\n\\n## Test Data Requirements\\n\\n### Git Repository Test Data\\n- Clean test repositories for each test scenario\\n- Pre-configured branch structures for workflow testing\\n- Sample commit histories for conflict simulation\\n- Invalid repository states for error testing\\n\\n### State Persistence Test Data\\n- Valid checkpoint files for restoration testing\\n- Corrupted checkpoint data for error handling\\n- Large state objects for performance testing\\n- Concurrent access scenarios for race condition testing\\n\\n### Secrets Management Test Data\\n- Test API keys and credentials (non-functional)\\n- Encrypted credential samples\\n- Access control configuration data\\n- Audit log sample data\\n\\n### Performance Test Data\\n- Large numbers of concurrent operations\\n- Extensive git histories for performance benchmarking\\n- Multiple checkpoint files for cleanup testing\\n- High-frequency state updates for stress testing\\n\\n## Mock Strategy\\n\\n### External Dependencies to Mock\\n- **Git Commands**: Mock all `git` CLI operations for unit tests\\n- **File System**: Mock file operations for isolated testing\\n- **External APIs**: Mock credential provider APIs\\n- **Network Operations**: Mock all external network calls\\n- **System Resources**: Mock system-level resource checks\\n\\n### Real Integration Points\\n- **Actual Git Repositories**: Use real git repos for integration tests\\n- **File System Storage**: Use real file storage for integration tests\\n- **Encryption Libraries**: Use real crypto libraries for security tests\\n- **Database Connections**: Use real database for state persistence tests\\n\\n## Performance Benchmarks\\n\\n### Git Operations Performance\\n- **Commit Creation**: < 2 seconds for standard commits\\n- **Branch Operations**: < 1 second for branch creation/switching\\n- **Merge Operations**: < 5 seconds for standard merges\\n- **History Analysis**: < 3 seconds for 1000 commit analysis\\n\\n### State Persistence Performance\\n- **Checkpoint Creation**: < 1 second for typical agent state\\n- **State Restoration**: < 2 seconds for complete recovery\\n- **Concurrent Access**: Handle 10 concurrent agents\\n- **Storage Efficiency**: < 10MB per checkpoint\\n\\n### Security Operations Performance\\n- **Credential Retrieval**: < 500ms for encrypted credential access\\n- **Access Validation**: < 100ms for permission checks\\n- **Audit Logging**: < 50ms for audit event recording\\n- **Encryption/Decryption**: < 200ms for typical credential sizes\\n\\n## Test Environment Requirements\\n\\n### Development Environment\\n- Git repository with test branches\\n- Local file system for state storage\\n- Mock credential providers\\n- Test databases for integration\\n\\n### CI/CD Environment  \\n- Automated test git repositories\\n- Containerized test environments\\n- Secure credential storage for integration tests\\n- Performance monitoring tools\\n\\n### Security Testing Environment\\n- Isolated network environment\\n- Security scanning tools\\n- Audit log analysis tools\\n- Penetration testing capabilities\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Unit Test Success\\n- 85% code coverage achieved\\n- All business logic functions tested\\n- Edge cases and error conditions covered\\n- Fast test execution (< 30 seconds total)\\n\\n### Integration Test Success\\n- All external integrations verified\\n- Real-world scenarios successfully tested\\n- Error handling validated with actual systems\\n- Performance benchmarks met\\n\\n### E2E Test Success\\n- Complete user workflows validated\\n- Recovery scenarios successfully tested\\n- Security controls verified\\n- System stability demonstrated\\n\\n### Overall Success\\n- Zero critical bugs in foundation infrastructure\\n- All performance benchmarks exceeded\\n- Security audit requirements satisfied\\n- Ready for Phase 2 feature development\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation Testing\\n\\n### High-Risk Areas\\n1. **Git Operation Conflicts**: Extensive testing of concurrent git operations\\n2. **State Corruption**: Comprehensive testing of recovery mechanisms\\n3. **Security Vulnerabilities**: Thorough security testing and penetration testing\\n4. **Performance Degradation**: Load testing and performance monitoring\\n5. **Integration Failures**: Extensive testing of external system integrations\\n\\n### Contingency Testing\\n- Backup system validation\\n- Rollback procedure testing\\n- Disaster recovery scenario testing\\n- Performance degradation response testing\\n\\nThis comprehensive test strategy ensures the foundation infrastructure is robust, secure, and performant enough to support all future milestone development."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-5-20251101', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 91.2%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.0\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
