{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:28:46", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-bd19ec0f-b65b-459f-9c76-86f1e5f88010', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Memory Leak Investigation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TsNTDY1oTQDjiuwDt6cikK', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TsNTDY1oTQDjiuwDt6cikK', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Memory Leak Investigation - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nInvestigate and address potential memory leaks in the ensemble agent system to ensure completed agents are not held in execution memory (RAM) longer than necessary, preventing memory bloat and system crashes.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Objectives\\n1. **Audit Current Memory Management**: Analyze how agents are stored and cleaned up in the system\\n2. **Identify Memory Leaks**: Find where completed agents or their data might be persisting in RAM\\n3. **Implement Proper Cleanup**: Ensure agents are properly garbage collected after completion\\n4. **Validate Memory Efficiency**: Verify the system maintains stable memory usage over time\\n\\n### Secondary Objectives\\n- Document memory management best practices for the system\\n- Implement monitoring for memory usage patterns\\n- Optimize existing memory cleanup mechanisms\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Agent runtime memory management\\n- SwarmStateManager memory efficiency\\n- Parallel executor resource cleanup\\n- Message history memory usage\\n- Tool execution result storage\\n- Agent conversation history cleanup\\n- ThreadPoolExecutor resource management\\n- Activity tracker memory usage\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Database storage optimization (focus is on RAM usage)\\n- Frontend JavaScript memory leaks\\n- OS-level memory management\\n- External API connection pooling (unless directly related to agent cleanup)\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **No Memory Leaks**: Completed agents and their resources are properly released from RAM\\n2. **Stable Memory Usage**: System memory usage remains stable during long-running operations\\n3. **Efficient Cleanup**: Agent resources are cleaned up within 30 seconds of completion\\n4. **Documentation**: Clear documentation of memory management practices\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- **No Service Disruption**: Investigation and fixes must not break existing functionality\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Changes must maintain compatibility with existing agent definitions\\n- **Performance**: Memory cleanup must not significantly impact agent execution performance\\n\\n## Current System Analysis\\n\\n### Existing Memory Management Mechanisms\\nBased on initial investigation, the system already has several memory management features:\\n\\n1. **SQLite-Backed State Management**\\n   - SwarmStateManager uses SQLite for persistence instead of keeping all state in memory\\n   - Thread-local database connections with proper cleanup\\n   - Message history stored in database, not RAM\\n\\n2. **Message History Pruning**\\n   - AgentRuntime._prune_message_history() limits conversation history\\n   - Configured with max_message_history = 50 messages\\n   - Prunes every 10 iterations (prune_frequency = 10)\\n\\n3. **ThreadPoolExecutor Management**\\n   - ParallelAgentExecutor uses ThreadPoolExecutor with configurable max_workers\\n   - Provides shutdown() method for proper cleanup\\n   - Tracks running_tasks and removes completed ones\\n\\n4. **Database Connection Management**\\n   - SwarmStateManager uses context managers for database connections\\n   - Thread-local connections to avoid sharing issues\\n   - WAL mode enabled for better concurrency\\n\\n### Potential Memory Leak Areas\\n1. **Agent Instance Retention**: Check if completed agent objects are held in global collections\\n2. **Circular References**: Agent parent/child relationships might create reference cycles\\n3. **Tool Result Caching**: Tool execution results might accumulate without cleanup\\n4. **Event Bus Accumulation**: Unprocessed events might pile up in memory\\n5. **Metrics Tracker State**: Performance metrics might accumulate without bounds\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Phase 1: Memory Audit\\n- Profile current memory usage patterns\\n- Identify objects that persist after agent completion\\n- Check for circular references or weak reference opportunities\\n- Monitor memory growth during agent execution cycles\\n\\n### Phase 2: Cleanup Implementation\\n- Add explicit cleanup methods to agent classes\\n- Implement weak references where appropriate\\n- Add memory monitoring and alerting\\n- Enhance existing pruning mechanisms\\n\\n### Phase 3: Validation\\n- Load testing with many sequential agent executions\\n- Memory profiling to verify stable usage\\n- Performance benchmarking to ensure no regression\\n- Documentation of memory management patterns\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The system is primarily experiencing issues with RAM usage, not disk storage\\n- Memory leaks are occurring in the Python runtime, not in external dependencies\\n- The issue affects long-running processes more than short-lived executions\\n- Existing SQLite persistence mechanism is working correctly"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01P2f3Qemq51AFGW7rZ9FQfy', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Memory Leak Investigation - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nInvestigate and address potential memory leaks in the ensemble agent system to ensure completed agents are not held in execution memory longer than necessary.\n\n## Milestone 1: Memory Audit and Analysis\n**Duration**: 2-3 days  \n**Priority**: High  \n\n### Objective\nProfile current memory usage patterns and identify specific memory leak sources in the agent system.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Memory profiling tool implementation\n2. Memory usage baseline documentation\n3. Circular reference detection analysis\n4. Object retention analysis report\n5. Hotspot identification for memory accumulation\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Memory profiling tool can track agent lifecycle memory usage\n- [ ] Baseline memory usage documented for normal operations\n- [ ] Identified all objects persisting after agent completion\n- [ ] Documented specific memory leak locations with evidence\n- [ ] Performance impact of profiling measured and acceptable\n\n### Dependencies\n- None (starting milestone)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: Cleanup Implementation\n**Duration**: 3-4 days  \n**Priority**: High  \n\n### Objective\nImplement proper cleanup mechanisms for identified memory leaks and enhance existing memory management.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Enhanced agent cleanup methods\n2. Weak reference implementations where appropriate\n3. Improved message history pruning\n4. Tool result cleanup mechanisms\n5. Event bus memory management\n6. Metrics tracker bounded storage\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All agent instances properly cleaned up within 30 seconds of completion\n- [ ] Circular references broken using weak references\n- [ ] Tool execution results have bounded memory usage\n- [ ] Event bus prevents unbounded accumulation\n- [ ] Metrics tracking uses rolling windows or periodic cleanup\n- [ ] No regression in agent execution performance\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 1 (requires analysis results to know what to fix)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 3: Monitoring and Validation\n**Duration**: 2-3 days  \n**Priority**: Medium  \n\n### Objective\nImplement monitoring systems and validate that memory leaks are resolved through comprehensive testing.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Memory monitoring dashboard/alerts\n2. Load testing framework for memory validation\n3. Automated memory regression tests\n4. Performance benchmarking suite\n5. Memory management documentation\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Monitoring system tracks memory usage trends\n- [ ] Load testing shows stable memory usage over 1000+ agent executions\n- [ ] Memory usage returns to baseline after agent completion\n- [ ] Performance benchmarks show <5% execution time regression\n- [ ] Complete documentation of memory management practices\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 2 (requires cleanup implementations to validate)\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### High Risk Areas\n1. **ThreadPoolExecutor Management**: Complex lifecycle with potential for resource leaks\n2. **Agent Parent/Child Relationships**: Circular references between related agents\n3. **Tool Result Caching**: Accumulation without bounds checking\n\n### Mitigation Strategies\n1. Implement explicit shutdown procedures for all executors\n2. Use weak references for parent/child relationships\n3. Add bounded caches with LRU eviction policies\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Memory usage remains stable (<5% growth) during long-running operations\n- Agent cleanup completes within 30 seconds\n- No detectable memory leaks after 1000+ agent executions\n- System performance regression <5%\n- Zero service disruptions during implementation'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01P2f3Qemq51AFGW7rZ9FQfy', 'content': '{"succ