{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:29:48", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-caefdcad-b94f-44fd-a274-2ff052f0f71d', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure. Create the recovery_agent.md agent definition file in leadership/ directory, implement input/output validation schemas using Pydantic, create validation utility functions, and integrate validation into the agent spawn pipeline. The Recovery Agent accepts recovery task information and spawns Executive Directors to handle recovered jobs. Key files: src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership/recovery_agent.md (new), src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py (new), src/ensemble/runtime/validation/agent_validator.py (new). See /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md for detailed task breakdown and /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md for test strategy.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership",\n  "test_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/tests",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FvaeawYNVpQwiGpczQfjFz', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DpLKavYVfPpXQbUYJavBzS', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UHfgtmnRdEjnEcxxLkdCyr', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Mdq6JpZtDz9Z99yffVskc5', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FvaeawYNVpQwiGpczQfjFz', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Backend Tasks - Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis milestone establishes the foundation for agent-based recovery by creating the Recovery Agent definition and implementing input/output format validation. This is the foundational work that enables recovered jobs to appear in the main agent hierarchy.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n\\n### Task 1.1: Create Recovery Agent Definition File\\n**Description**: Create the `recovery_agent.md` agent definition file in the leadership directory following the standard agent definition format.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- File created at `src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- Contains all required sections: Purpose, Instructions, Permissions, Input Format, Output Format, Termination Conditions\\n- Input format matches specification (recovery_task object + output_directory)\\n- Output format matches specification (status, recovery_id, spawned_executive_id, etc.)\\n- Permissions explicitly set: `can_spawn: [\\"leadership/executive_director\\"]`, `can_write_code: false`, `can_write_tests: false`\\n- Instructions clearly define: receive recovery task \\u2192 spawn Executive Director \\u2192 monitor completion \\u2192 report status\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Follow existing agent definition patterns from `docs/agents/leadership/`\\n- Include recovery-specific workflow steps\\n- Document error handling expectations\\n- Specify metadata requirements for recovery tracking\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 1.2: Create Recovery Agent Input Validation Schema\\n**Description**: Create Pydantic models for validating Recovery Agent input format, ensuring all required fields are present and correctly typed.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryTaskInput` created for the recovery_task object\\n- Fields validated: original_agent_id (str), original_session_id (str), agent_type (str), agent_name (str), input_data (dict), failure_reason (str), recovery_strategy (str), recovery_attempt (int)\\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryAgentInput` created wrapping recovery_task + output_directory\\n- Validation includes: required field checks, type validation, string min/max lengths where appropriate\\n- All validation errors return clear messages indicating which field failed and why\\n- Unit tests cover: valid input, missing fields, wrong types, invalid values\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1 (definition file provides specification)\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Create in `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py` (new file)\\n- Use Pydantic v2 syntax with Field validators\\n- recovery_strategy should be an enum: [\\"retry\\", \\"enhance_prompt\\", \\"escalate\\"]\\n- recovery_attempt must be positive integer\\n- input_data is dict with no schema (flexible for any agent type)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 1.3: Create Recovery Agent Output Validation Schema\\n**Description**: Create Pydantic models for validating Recovery Agent output format, ensuring consistent response structure.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryAgentOutput` created\\n- Fields validated: status (enum: success/failed/needs_user_input), recovery_id (str), spawned_executive_id (str), original_agent_id (str), message (str), self_analysis (str)\\n- All fields required except self_analysis (optional)\\n- Status enum properly defined and enforced\\n- Unit tests cover: valid output, missing fields, invalid status values\\n- Output validation integrated with agent response handling\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1 (definition file provides specification)\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Add to `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py`\\n- Status enum: `RecoveryStatus = Literal[\\"success\\", \\"failed\\", \\"needs_user_input\\"]`\\n- recovery_id and spawned_executive_id should follow UUID format (add validator)\\n- self_analysis defaults to empty string if not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 2: Validation Infrastructure\\n\\n### Task 2.1: Create Validation Utility for Agent I/O\\n**Description**: Create a generic utility function that validates agent inputs and outputs against their defined schemas, usable by the Recovery Agent and future agents.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Function `validate_agent_input(agent_type: str, input_data: dict) -> tuple[bool, dict|str]` created\\n- Function `validate_agent_output(agent_type: str, output_data: dict) -> tuple[bool, dict|str]` created\\n- Functions return (success: bool, validated_data_or_error_message)\\n- Schema registry maps agent types to their Pydantic models\\n- Recovery Agent schemas registered in the registry\\n- Unit tests cover: valid data, invalid data, unknown agent type, malformed JSON\\n- Error messages are descriptive and actionable\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2, Task 1.3\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Create `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/agent_validator.py` (new file)\\n- Schema registry: `AGENT_SCHEMAS = {\\"leadership/recovery_agent\\": {\\"input\\": RecoveryAgentInput, \\"output\\": RecoveryAgentOutput}}`\\n- Handle Pydantic ValidationError and return formatted error messages\\n- Cache schema instances for performance\\n- Future-proof: allow dynamic schema registration\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 2.2: Integrate Validation into Agent Spawn Pipeline\\n**Description**: Hook the validation utility into the agent spawning process so that input validation occurs before spawning and output validation occurs after completion.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- `spawn_agent` function validates input using `validate_agent_input` before spawning\\n- If validation fails, spawn_agent returns error without spawning agent\\n- Agent completion handler validates output using `validate_agent_output`\\n- If output validation fails, log warning but don\'t block (agent already completed)\\n- Validation errors logged with agent_type, input/output data, and specific validation failure\\n- Integration tests verify validation occurs at correct points in lifecycle\\n- Metrics tracked: validation_failures_total (by agent_type, validation_type: input/output)\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Modify `src/ensemble/runtime/agent_spawner.py` (or equivalent spawning logic)\\n- Add validation call before `Agent.create()` or equivalent\\n- Add validation call in agent completion callback/handler\\n- Use existing logging infrastructure for validation errors\\n- Consider: Add `skip_validation=False` parameter for backwards compatibility during rollout\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 3: Testing Infrastructure\\n\\n### Task 3.1: Create Recovery Agent Test Fixtures\\n**Description**: Create pytest fixtures and test data generators for Recovery Agent testing.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Fixture `valid_recovery_task_input()` generates valid RecoveryAgentInput\\n- Fixture `invalid_recovery_task_input(field: str)` generates input with specified invalid field\\n- Fixture `valid_recovery_agent_output()` generates valid RecoveryAgentOutput\\n- Test data includes edge cases: very long strings, special characters, boundary integers\\n- Fixtures parameterizable (e.g., override specific fields)\\n- Documentation explains how to use fixtures in tests\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2, Task 1.3\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Create `tests/fixtures/recovery_agent_fixtures.py`\\n- Use factory pattern: `def recovery_task_factory(**overrides) -> dict`\\n- Include fixtures for all recovery strategies\\n- Include fixtures for all status values\\n- Ensure generated UUIDs are valid format\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 3.2: Create Validation Test Suite\\n**Description**: Comprehensive test suite for input/output validation covering all schemas and edge cases.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Test file `tests/unit/test_recovery_validation.py` created\\n- Tests for RecoveryTaskInput: valid input, each required field missing, each field wrong type, boundary values\\n- Tests for RecoveryAgentInput: valid input, missing output_directory, invalid paths\\n- Tests for RecoveryAgentOutput: valid output, each status value, missing required fields, invalid UUIDs\\n- Tests for validate_agent_input: valid, invalid, unknown agent type, malformed data\\n- Tests for validate_agent_output: valid, invalid, unknown agent type\\n- All tests pass with >95% code coverage on validation modules\\n- Tests use fixtures from Task 3.1\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1, Task 2.1\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Use pytest parametrize for testing multiple invalid field scenarios\\n- Test error messages are descriptive\\n- Test that Pydantic validation errors are properly caught and formatted\\n- Test edge cases: empty strings, null values, extremely large integers\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 3.3: Create Integration Test for Agent Spawn Validation\\n**Description**: Integration test verifying validation occurs correctly during the agent spawn lifecycle.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Test file `tests/integration/test_spawn_validation.py` created\\n- Test: Valid input passes validation and agent spawns successfully\\n- Test: Invalid input fails validation and agent does not spawn\\n- Test: Valid output passes validation silently\\n- Test: Invalid output logs warning but doesn\'t block\\n- Test: Unknown agent type skips validation (no schema registered)\\n- Mock agent spawning to avoid full agent execution\\n- Verify validation metrics are incremented correctly\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.2, Task 3.1\\n\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Use pytest-mock for mocking spawn_agent internals\\n- Mock agent completion to control output validation testing\\n- Capture logs and verify validation error messages appear\\n- Mock metrics/telemetry and assert validation_failures_total incremented\\n- Test both sync and async spawn paths if applicable\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Task Group 4: Documentation & Examples\\n\\n### Task 4.1: Create Recovery Agent Usage Documentation\\n**Description**: Write documentation explaining how to use the Recovery Agent, including input/output examples and integration guidance.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Documentation file `docs/recovery_agent_usage.md` created\\n- Sections: Overview, Input Format (with examples), Output Format (with examples), Common Errors, Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Includes complete JSON examples of valid input and output\\n- Documents all recovery strategies and when to use each\\n- Explains error messages and how to fix validation failures\\n- Links to agent definition file and validation schemas\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1, Task 1.2, Task 1.3\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Use real examples from test fixtures\\n- Include code snippets showing how to spawn Recovery Agent\\n- Add flowchart showing Recovery Agent workflow\\n- Include troubleshooting section with common validation errors\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Task 4.2: Create Validation Schema Documentation\\n**Description**: Write developer documentation for the validation infrastructure, enabling other agents to adopt validation.\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Documentation file `docs/agent_validation.md` created\\n- Sections: Overview, Creating Schemas, Registering Schemas, Testing Validation, Best Practices\\n- Step-by-step guide for adding validation to new agent types\\n- Example showing full validation implementation for a sample agent\\n- Documents the validation utility API\\n- Explains validation timing (pre-spawn, post-completion)\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1, Task 2.2\\n\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n\\n**Technical Details**:\\n- Include code examples for creating Pydantic schemas\\n- Show how to register schemas in AGENT_SCHEMAS registry\\n- Document when to use strict vs lenient validation\\n- Explain error handling patterns\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Total Tasks**: 11\\n**Task Groups**: 4\\n\\n**Dependencies Chain**:\\n1. Foundation: Task 1.1 (agent definition)\\n2. Schemas: Task 1.2, 1.3 (input/output schemas)\\n3. Validation Infrastructure: Task 2.1 \\u2192 Task 2.2 (validation utilities \\u2192 integration)\\n4. Testing: Task 3.1 \\u2192 Task 3.2, Task 3.3 (fixtures \\u2192 tests)\\n5. Documentation: Task 4.1, Task 4.2 (parallel, depend on implementation tasks)\\n\\n**Critical Path**: \\nTask 1.1 \\u2192 Task 1.2 \\u2192 Task 2.1 \\u2192 Task 2.2 \\u2192 Task 3.3\\n\\n**Estimated Complexity**:\\n- Simple: 4 tasks\\n- Medium: 6 tasks\\n- Complex: 0 tasks\\n\\n**Key Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership/recovery_agent.md` - Agent definition\\n2. `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py` - Pydantic validation models\\n3. `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/agent_validator.py` - Validation utility\\n4. Integration with spawn pipeline for automatic validation\\n5. Comprehensive test suite with >95% coverage\\n6. Developer documentation for recovery agent and validation infrastructure\\n\\n**Ready for Handoff**: Yes - All tasks are well-defined, have clear acceptance criteria, and can be implemented via TDD by the TDD Coordinator.\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DpLKavYVfPpXQbUYJavBzS', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Tasks - Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure\\n\\n## Overview\\nTest strategy for validating the Recovery Agent definition, input/output format validation, and permission enforcement. This milestone is foundational - all tests focus on ensuring the Recovery Agent is correctly defined and can be validated.\\n\\n## Test Coverage Goals\\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 95% for validation schemas and utilities\\n- **Integration Coverage**: 100% of agent spawn validation pipeline\\n- **Edge Case Coverage**: All boundary conditions and error scenarios\\n\\n## Testing Framework Stack\\n- **Backend**: pytest with pytest-mock for mocking\\n- **Validation**: Pydantic model testing patterns\\n- **Fixtures**: Factory-based test data generation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Unit Tests\\n\\n### Test Task T1.1: Recovery Agent Input Validation Tests\\n**Description**: Test RecoveryTaskInput and RecoveryAgentInput Pydantic model validation.\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n1. `test_valid_recovery_task_input_passes_validation`\\n   - Valid input with all required fields passes\\n   - Validated object has correct field values\\n   \\n2. `test_missing_original_agent_id_fails`\\n   - Missing original_agent_id raises ValidationError\\n   - Error message mentions \\"original_agent_id\\"\\n   \\n3. `test_missing_original_session_id_fails`\\n   - Missing original_session_id raises ValidationError\\n   \\n4. `test_missing_agent_type_fails`\\n   - Missing agent_type raises ValidationError\\n   \\n5. `test_missing_input_data_fails`\\n   - Missing input_data raises ValidationError\\n   \\n6. `test_missing_failure_reason_fails`\\n   - Missing failure_reason raises ValidationError\\n   \\n7. `test_missing_recovery_strategy_fails`\\n   - Missing recovery_strategy raises ValidationError\\n   \\n8. `test_invalid_recovery_strategy_fails`\\n   - Invalid strategy value (not in enum) raises ValidationError\\n   \\n9. `test_missing_recovery_attempt_fails`\\n   - Missing recovery_attempt raises ValidationError\\n   \\n10. `test_negative_recovery_attempt_fails`\\n    - Negative recovery_attempt raises ValidationError\\n    \\n11. `test_zero_recovery_attempt_fails`\\n    - Zero recovery_attempt raises ValidationError (must be positive)\\n    \\n12. `test_input_data_accepts_dict`\\n    - input_data can be any dictionary\\n    - Nested dicts work correctly\\n    \\n13. `test_missing_output_directory_fails`\\n    - RecoveryAgentInput without output_directory fails\\n    \\n14. `test_valid_recovery_agent_input_passes`\\n    - Complete RecoveryAgentInput with valid recovery_task passes\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All test cases pass\\n- Error messages are descriptive\\n- 100% line coverage on input schemas\\n\\n**File**: `tests/unit/test_recovery_agent_input_validation.py`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Test Task T1.2: Recovery Agent Output Validation Tests\\n**Description**: Test RecoveryAgentOutput Pydantic model validation.\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n1. `test_valid_recovery_output_passes`\\n   - Valid output with all required fields passes\\n   \\n2. `test_status_success_is_valid`\\n   - status=\\"success\\" passes validation\\n   \\n3. `test_status_failed_is_valid`\\n   - status=\\"failed\\" passes validation\\n   \\n4. `test_status_needs_user_input_is_valid`\\n   - status=\\"needs_user_input\\" passes validation\\n   \\n5. `test_invalid_status_fails`\\n   - Invalid status value raises ValidationError\\n   \\n6. `test_missing_status_fails`\\n   - Missing status field raises ValidationError\\n   \\n7. `test_missing_recovery_id_fails`\\n   - Missing recovery_id raises ValidationError\\n   \\n8. `test_missing_spawned_executive_id_fails`\\n   - Missing spawned_executive_id raises ValidationError\\n   \\n9. `test_missing_original_agent_id_fails`\\n   - Missing original_agent_id raises ValidationError\\n   \\n10. `test_missing_message_fails`\\n    - Missing message field raises ValidationError\\n    \\n11. `test_self_analysis_optional`\\n    - Output without self_analysis passes\\n    - self_analysis defaults to empty string\\n    \\n12. `test_invalid_uuid_format_recovery_id_fails`\\n    - Non-UUID recovery_id raises ValidationError\\n    \\n13. `test_invalid_uuid_format_executive_id_fails`\\n    - Non-UUID spawned_executive_id raises ValidationError\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All test cases pass\\n- UUID format validation working\\n- Status enum properly enforced\\n- 100% line coverage on output schema\\n\\n**File**: `tests/unit/test_recovery_agent_output_validation.py`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Test Task T1.3: Validation Utility Function Tests\\n**Description**: Test the validate_agent_input and validate_agent_output utility functions.\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n1. `test_validate_agent_input_valid_data_returns_success`\\n   - Valid recovery agent input returns (True, validated_data)\\n   \\n2. `test_validate_agent_input_invalid_data_returns_failure`\\n   - Invalid input returns (False, error_message)\\n   \\n3. `test_validate_agent_input_unknown_agent_type_returns_failure`\\n   - Unknown agent type returns (False, \\"no schema registered\\")\\n   \\n4. `test_validate_agent_input_malformed_json_returns_failure`\\n   - Malformed JSON returns (False, error_message)\\n   \\n5. `test_validate_agent_output_valid_data_returns_success`\\n   - Valid recovery agent output returns (True, validated_data)\\n   \\n6. `test_validate_agent_output_invalid_data_returns_failure`\\n   - Invalid output returns (False, error_message)\\n   \\n7. `test_validate_agent_output_unknown_agent_type_returns_failure`\\n   - Unknown agent type returns (False, \\"no schema registered\\")\\n   \\n8. `test_error_message_includes_field_name`\\n   - Error messages include which field failed validation\\n   \\n9. `test_error_message_includes_reason`\\n   - Error messages explain why validation failed\\n   \\n10. `test_schema_registry_contains_recovery_agent`\\n    - AGENT_SCHEMAS has \\"leadership/recovery_agent\\" entry\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All test cases pass\\n- Error messages are actionable\\n- Schema registry properly configured\\n\\n**File**: `tests/unit/test_validation_utility.py`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Test Task T1.4: Recovery Agent Definition Parsing Tests\\n**Description**: Test that the recovery_agent.md file can be parsed and contains required sections.\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n1. `test_agent_definition_file_exists`\\n   - File exists at expected path\\n   \\n2. `test_agent_definition_contains_purpose_section`\\n   - File contains \\"## Purpose\\" section\\n   \\n3. `test_agent_definition_contains_instructions_section`\\n   - File contains \\"## Instructions\\" section\\n   \\n4. `test_agent_definition_contains_permissions_section`\\n   - File contains permissions section\\n   \\n5. `test_agent_definition_can_spawn_executive_director_only`\\n   - can_spawn includes \\"leadership/executive_director\\"\\n   - can_spawn does NOT include other agent types\\n   \\n6. `test_agent_definition_cannot_write_code`\\n   - can_write_code: false\\n   \\n7. `test_agent_definition_input_format_section`\\n   - File contains \\"## Input Format\\" section\\n   \\n8. `test_agent_definition_output_format_section`\\n   - File contains \\"## Output Format\\" section\\n   \\n9. `test_agent_definition_input_matches_schema`\\n   - Input format in definition matches Pydantic schema fields\\n   \\n10. `test_agent_definition_output_matches_schema`\\n    - Output format in definition matches Pydantic schema fields\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Agent definition follows standard format\\n- Permissions are correctly restricted\\n- Schema matches documented format\\n\\n**File**: `tests/unit/test_recovery_agent_definition.py`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Integration Tests\\n\\n### Test Task T2.1: Agent Spawn Validation Integration Tests\\n**Description**: Test that validation is properly integrated into the agent spawn pipeline.\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n1. `test_spawn_recovery_agent_with_valid_input_succeeds`\\n   - spawn_agent with valid input returns success\\n   - Agent is created\\n   \\n2. `test_spawn_recovery_agent_with_invalid_input_fails`\\n   - spawn_agent with invalid input returns error\\n   - Agent is NOT created\\n   - Error message indicates validation failure\\n   \\n3. `test_spawn_agent_invalid_input_does_not_spawn`\\n   - Verify agent creation is not called when validation fails\\n   - Mock agent creation to verify not called\\n   \\n4. `test_spawn_agent_validation_error_logged`\\n   - Validation failures are logged\\n   - Log contains agent_type and validation error\\n   \\n5. `test_agent_output_validation_on_completion`\\n   - Agent completion triggers output validation\\n   - Valid output passes silently\\n   \\n6. `test_invalid_output_logs_warning_but_succeeds`\\n   - Invalid output logs warning\\n   - Agent completion still succeeds (not blocked)\\n   \\n7. `test_validation_metrics_incremented_on_failure`\\n   - Input validation failure increments metric\\n   - Output validation failure increments metric\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Validation occurs at correct lifecycle points\\n- Invalid input prevents agent spawning\\n- Invalid output is logged but doesn\'t block\\n- Metrics properly tracked\\n\\n**File**: `tests/integration/test_spawn_validation_integration.py`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Test Task T2.2: Recovery Agent Permission Enforcement Tests\\n**Description**: Test that Recovery Agent can only spawn Executive Director.\\n\\n**Test Cases**:\\n1. `test_recovery_agent_can_spawn_executive_director`\\n   - Recovery Agent spawning Executive Director succeeds\\n   \\n2. `test_recovery_agent_cannot_spawn_dev_manager`\\n   - Recovery Agent spawning Dev Manager is rejected\\n   \\n3. `test_recovery_agent_cannot_spawn_code_writer`\\n   - Recovery Agent spawning code_writer is rejected\\n   \\n4. `test_recovery_agent_cannot_spawn_coordinator`\\n   - Recovery Agent spawning any coordinator is rejected\\n   \\n5. `test_permission_error_message_clear`\\n   - Permission denial error clearly states what agent can/cannot spawn\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Permission enforcement working correctly\\n- Only Executive Director can be spawned\\n- Clear error messages on permission denial\\n\\n**File**: `tests/integration/test_recovery_agent_permissions.py`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test Fixtures\\n\\n### Test Task T3.1: Create Recovery Agent Test Fixtures\\n**Description**: Create reusable test fixtures for Recovery Agent testing.\\n\\n**Fixtures to Create**:\\n1. `valid_recovery_task_input()` - Returns valid RecoveryTaskInput dict\\n2. `valid_recovery_agent_input()` - Returns valid RecoveryAgentInput dict\\n3. `valid_recovery_agent_output()` - Returns valid RecoveryAgentOutput dict\\n4. `recovery_task_factory(**overrides)` - Factory to create inputs with overrides\\n5. `invalid_recovery_input_missing_field(field_name)` - Input with specified field missing\\n6. `invalid_recovery_strategy_input()` - Input with invalid recovery strategy\\n7. `all_recovery_strategies()` - List of all valid recovery strategy values\\n8. `all_recovery_statuses()` - List of all valid status values\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Fixtures are reusable across all test files\\n- Factory pattern allows easy customization\\n- Documentation explains usage\\n\\n**File**: `tests/fixtures/recovery_agent_fixtures.py`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Total Test Tasks**: 8\\n- Unit Tests: 4 tasks (T1.1-T1.4)\\n- Integration Tests: 2 tasks (T2.1-T2.2)\\n- Test Fixtures: 1 task (T3.1)\\n\\n**Estimated Test Cases**: 62+\\n\\n**Critical Path**:\\n1. T3.1 (fixtures) - foundation for all other tests\\n2. T1.1, T1.2 (schema validation tests) - parallel\\n3. T1.3 (utility tests) - depends on schema tests\\n4. T1.4 (definition parsing) - depends on agent definition creation\\n5. T2.1, T2.2 (integration tests) - depends on implementation\\n\\n**Coverage Target**: 95% for all validation code\\n\\n**Test File Structure**:\\n```\\ntests/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 fixtures/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 recovery_agent_fixtures.py\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 unit/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 test_recovery_agent_input_validation.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 test_recovery_agent_output_validation.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 test_validation_utility.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 test_recovery_agent_definition.py\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration/\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 test_spawn_validation_integration.py\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 test_recovery_agent_permissions.py\\n```\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UHfgtmnRdEjnEcxxLkdCyr', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Memory Leak Investigation - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nInvestigate and address potential memory leaks in the ensemble agent system to ensure completed agents are not held in execution memory (RAM) longer than necessary, preventing memory bloat and system crashes.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Objectives\\n1. **Audit Current Memory Management**: Analyze how agents are stored and cleaned up in the system\\n2. **Identify Memory Leaks**: Find where completed agents or their data might be persisting in RAM\\n3. **Implement Proper Cleanup**: Ensure agents are properly garbage collected after completion\\n4. **Validate Memory Efficiency**: Verify the system maintains stable memory usage over time\\n\\n### Secondary Objectives\\n- Document memory management best practices for the system\\n- Implement monitoring for memory usage patterns\\n- Optimize existing memory cleanup mechanisms\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Agent runtime memory management\\n- SwarmStateManager memory efficiency\\n- Parallel executor resource cleanup\\n- Message history memory usage\\n- Tool execution result storage\\n- Agent conversation history cleanup\\n- ThreadPoolExecutor resource management\\n- Activity tracker memory usage\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Database storage optimization (focus is on RAM usage)\\n- Frontend JavaScript memory leaks\\n- OS-level memory management\\n- External API connection pooling (unless directly related to agent cleanup)\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **No Memory Leaks**: Completed agents and their resources are properly released from RAM\\n2. **Stable Memory Usage**: System memory usage remains stable during long-running operations\\n3. **Efficient Cleanup**: Agent resources are cleaned up within 30 seconds of completion\\n4. **Documentation**: Clear documentation of memory management practices\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- **No Service Disruption**: Investigation and fixes must not break existing functionality\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Changes must maintain compatibility with existing agent definitions\\n- **Performance**: Memory cleanup must not significantly impact agent execution performance\\n\\n## Current System Analysis\\n\\n### Existing Memory Management Mechanisms\\nBased on initial investigation, the system already has several memory management features:\\n\\n1. **SQLite-Backed State Management**\\n   - SwarmStateManager uses SQLite for persistence instead of keeping all state in memory\\n   - Thread-local database connections with proper cleanup\\n   - Message history stored in database, not RAM\\n\\n2. **Message History Pruning**\\n   - AgentRuntime._prune_message_history() limits conversation history\\n   - Configured with max_message_history = 50 messages\\n   - Prunes every 10 iterations (prune_frequency = 10)\\n\\n3. **ThreadPoolExecutor Management**\\n   - ParallelAgentExecutor uses ThreadPoolExecutor with configurable max_workers\\n   - Provides shutdown() method for proper cleanup\\n   - Tracks running_tasks and removes completed ones\\n\\n4. **Database Connection Management**\\n   - SwarmStateManager uses context managers for database connections\\n   - Thread-local connections to avoid sharing issues\\n   - WAL mode enabled for better concurrency\\n\\n### Potential Memory Leak Areas\\n1. **Agent Instance Retention**: Check if completed agent objects are held in global collections\\n2. **Circular References**: Agent parent/child relationships might create reference cycles\\n3. **Tool Result Caching**: Tool execution results might accumulate without cleanup\\n4. **Event Bus Accumulation**: Unprocessed events might pile up in memory\\n5. **Metrics Tracker State**: Performance metrics might accumulate without bounds\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Phase 1: Memory Audit\\n- Profile current memory usage patterns\\n- Identify objects that persist after agent completion\\n- Check for circular references or weak reference opportunities\\n- Monitor memory growth during agent execution cycles\\n\\n### Phase 2: Cleanup Implementation\\n- Add explicit cleanup methods to agent classes\\n- Implement weak references where appropriate\\n- Add memory monitoring and alerting\\n- Enhance existing pruning mechanisms\\n\\n### Phase 3: Validation\\n- Load testing with many sequential agent executions\\n- Memory profiling to verify stable usage\\n- Performance benchmarking to ensure no regression\\n- Documentation of memory management patterns\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The system is primarily experiencing issues with RAM usage, not disk storage\\n- Memory leaks are occurring in the Python runtime, not in external dependencies\\n- The issue affects long-running processes more than short-lived executions\\n- Existing SQLite persistence mechanism is working correctly"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Mdq6JpZtDz9Z99yffVskc5', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/activity-tracking-bug-fixes", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["logs/ensemble-backend.log.4", "output/", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output