{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:30:39", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-201d68c7-4580-4b32-8ae6-2c21a3e6a4bd', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "task_description": "Write comprehensive unit tests for WriteFileTool activity tracking functionality. Tests must cover: (1) Constructor accepts agent_id, agent_name, request_id parameters in addition to agent_definition, (2) execute() method records file generation via activity_tracker.record_file_generated() when context parameters are provided, passing agent_id, agent_name, request_id, file_path, and file_type, (3) Backward compatibility: execute() works normally when context parameters (agent_id, agent_name, request_id) are not provided to constructor, (4) File type detection correctly identifies file types for extensions: .py (python), .md (markdown), .js (javascript), .tsx (tsx), .ts (typescript), .json (json), .yaml (yaml). Use pytest. Mock AgentRuntime.get_activity_tracker() to return a mock activity tracker. Import WriteFileTool from src.runtime.agents.tools. Use pytest tmpdir fixture for temporary file writing. These tests should FAIL initially because WriteFileTool.__init__ currently only accepts agent_definition parameter and doesn\'t call activity_tracker.record_file_generated().",\n  "test_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/tests/runtime/agents/test_tools_activity_tracking.py",\n  "code_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/runtime/agents/tools.py",\n  "testing_framework": "pytest",\n  "coverage_target": "90%"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01